# Codex 5.5 xhigh implementation guidance: integrated geotechCLI extraction review UI

## What this implements

Create one unified UI for geotechnical report extraction review. The UI must not be two disconnected dashboards.

The same extracted borehole objects must drive:

- source report evidence overlay
- field cards and confidence scores
- deterministic borehole strip log
- source easting/northing and transformed map coordinates
- real map borehole markers
- CRS validation guardrails
- A-A′ stratigraphic cross-section
- coordinate table
- integrated JSON export
- validation and artifact panels

The generated files in this package are:

```text
geotechcli_integrated_review.html
IntegratedGeotechReviewPage.tsx
integrated_geotech_review_codex_guidance.md
```

Use the HTML as the visual reference and the TSX page as the Next.js implementation base.

---

## Core design principle

Do not create a “headless chicken” UI where the map, strip log, source page, and field cards use unrelated mock data.

Everything must read from one model:

```ts
type IntegratedReviewModel = {
  schemaVersion: "geotech.integrated_review.v1";

  run: {
    id: string;
    document: string;
    documentHash: string;
    providerProfile: string;
    models: {
      ocr: string;
      vision: string;
      text: string;
    };
    status: "accepted" | "review_recommended" | "review_required";
  };

  project: {
    name: string;
    country: string;
    site: string;
    inputCrs: string;
    inputCrsName: string;
    displayCrs: "EPSG:4326";
    displayCrsName: string;
    verticalDatum: string;
    crsTransformEngine: "pyproj" | "proj" | "proj4js";
  };

  quality: {
    overallConfidence: number;
    evidenceCoverage: number;
    depthMappingR2: number;
    warnings: string[];
  };

  boreholes: Borehole[];
};
```

Each borehole must contain extraction evidence, engineering data, and geospatial data:

```ts
type Borehole = {
  id: string;
  sourcePage: number;

  easting: number;
  northing: number;
  lat: number;
  lon: number;

  groundLevel: number;
  totalDepth: number;
  chainage: number;
  offset: number;
  confidence: number;

  evidence: {
    id: string;
    coords: string;
    gl: string;
    td: string;
  };

  strata: Stratum[];
  spt: SptRecord[];
  groundwater: GroundwaterRecord[];
};
```

