## UI layout requirements

The UI has three top-level views:

```text
1. Extraction review
2. Map + A-A′ section
3. Validation + JSON
```

### Extraction review view

Use a three-column layout on wide screens:

```text
[ Source report evidence ] [ Validated strip log ] [ Extracted fields ]
```

Collapse to one column below approximately 1400 px.

Requirements:

- Do not allow absolute-positioned evidence boxes to overlap panel borders.
- Use scrollable field list instead of letting field cards stretch the page.
- Source log overlay must be generated from the selected borehole object.
- Selecting a borehole from the map or section must update:
  - source page
  - strip log
  - field cards
  - selected evidence
  - JSON

### Map + section view

Use:

```text
[ Leaflet map ] [ CRS guardrail + selected borehole ]
[ Full-width A-A′ stratigraphic section ]
```

Requirements:

- Map markers use transformed WGS84 latitude/longitude.
- Source easting/northing must remain visible in selected borehole panel and table.
- CRS warning must remain visible below the map.
- Cross-section must be horizontally scrollable if needed.
- Do not compress the section until labels overlap.

### Validation + JSON view

Use:

```text
[ Validation workflow ] [ Integrated JSON ]
[ Coordinate table ] [ Provider contract ]
```

Requirements:

- Warnings must be specific and engineering-relevant.
- Integrated JSON must be the exact object driving the UI.
- Provider contract must make clear that GLM is the default profile, but the UI is provider-agnostic.

