## Professional A-A′ stratigraphic section requirements

The A-A′ section must not show boreholes as only plain vertical lines.

Each borehole should be drawn as a vertical mini borehole log column:

```text
- colored/hatch-filled stratum segments
- borehole ID label above the column
- total depth label below the column
- SPT markers and N values beside the column
- groundwater strike symbol beside the column
- active borehole highlight
```

Between boreholes, draw conceptual interpolated strata surfaces:

```text
- ground surface as green polyline
- strata polygons between borehole boundaries
- dashed contact lines or dashed polygon strokes for interpolated boundaries
- groundwater strikes as dashed blue polyline
```

Use elevation, not depth, for the cross-section:

```ts
topElevation = borehole.groundLevel - stratum.top;
baseElevation = borehole.groundLevel - stratum.base;
```

The section scale must be calculated from data:

```ts
const maxElev = Math.ceil(max(borehole.groundLevel) + 1);
const minElev = Math.floor(min(borehole.groundLevel - borehole.totalDepth) - 0.5);
```

Map chainage to x-coordinate:

```ts
x = sectionX0 + (borehole.chainage / maxChainage) * sectionWidth;
```

Map elevation to y-coordinate:

```ts
y = sectionY0 + ((maxElev - elevation) / (maxElev - minElev)) * sectionHeight;
```

The UI must label the cross-section as conceptual:

```text
Strata between boreholes are conceptual interpolations for review.
Directly extracted log columns are shown at borehole locations.
Interpolated surfaces must not be treated as design surfaces without engineering review.
```

